    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "39ee4c35_d376b4af",
        "filename": "chip/stm32/usb_pd_phy.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 143,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-07-19T00:48:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I went down this road for a little while but it started getting really messy. The problem is some places in usb_pd_phy.c really need port number, for determining which spi registers to use or for pd_tx_enable()/disable(), etc. So, in usb_pd_phy.c you end up converting from void *ctxt to port number in some functions. And then in usb_pd_protocol.c, some functions need port number, others need void *ctxt, and most need both. It gets really messy having these two things that are essentially the same piece of information. So, I was trying to keep it simple by just passing around port.",
      "parentUuid": "1980a8c3_22b443ba",
      "revId": "34dd82d73c2c06acef11f0fd3e0b027f3631ba29",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
